@page "/components/tree-view"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.TreeView

<DocsHeader Title="Tree view" Eyebrow="Data">
    <Lead>Folders, categories and org charts: nested items that open and close, with keyboard support.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    <code>StilTreeView</code> follows the WAI-ARIA tree pattern. The tree is one tab stop; the arrow keys move between
    items, Right opens an item or moves to its first child, Left closes it or moves to its parent, and Home and End
    jump to the first and last visible item. Enter or Space selects. For links in a side menu, use
    <a href="components/navigation#nav-groups">nav groups</a> instead.
</p>

<h2 id="basic">Items, icons and selection</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(ProjectFiles)">
    <p>
        <code>Items</code> are the top level and <code>Children</code> returns an item's children.
        <code>ItemText</code> is the text and <code>ItemIcon</code> a <a href="components/icons">Stil icon</a> name.
        Bind <code>@@bind-SelectedItem</code> to know which item is chosen, and <code>@@bind-ExpandedItems</code> to
        choose or save which items are open. Give the tree a <code>Label</code>.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="template">Templates</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Departments)">
    <p>
        <code>ItemTemplate</code> renders any content in a row; <code>context</code> is the item. <code>ExpandAll</code>
        opens every item at the start. Set <code>ItemKey</code> when the items are new objects after every load, so the
        selection and the open items are kept.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="render-modes">Render modes</h2>
<p>
    In static server rendering the tree shows its first state (<code>ExpandedItems</code> or <code>ExpandAll</code>).
    Opening, closing, the keyboard and selection need an interactive render mode.
</p>

